Date: Sat, 04 Oct 2026 09:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] P1-38 / U-58: batch continuation jobs must run the
 batch-start settings snapshot, not a live re-read

Finding U-58 (F:NF-01 — WINNER audit, fix-order P1-38, state OPEN at main
fe4f0a7):

    Batch continuation re-reads LIVE settings — targets planned once
    (batchTargets_ U-01) but currentSettings() called live for each
    continuation job.

runCommand()'s batch branch computes the whole job plan — the planned
targets AND the collision-checked settings — then run 1 uses that
snapshot. But every continuation job in onProcessFinished() (runs 2..N)
rebuilt its argv from a LIVE currentSettings() call. Any Actions-tab state
that changed between completions (the setBusy/disabled-UI locks cover the
direct edits, not programmatic panel changes, session-restore timing, or
panel signals) silently rewrote the rest of the batch — the settings-twin
of U-45's closed output-destination hole: a job mutated after its plan was
validated, with the UI still showing the old plan.

Fix — the settings join the plan, where they always belonged:

  * MainWindow.h: new member gs::Settings batchSettings_ — read only while
    batchIndex_ >= 0 (the continuation condition), written once per batch.
  * runCommand() batch branch: batchSettings_ = settings right after the
    verified plan, beside the other per-batch planning state.
  * onProcessFinished() continuation: gs::Settings one = batchSettings_
    instead of the live re-read.

Header/application note (honesty line — this hunk is labelled, not hidden):
the continuation hunk and the MainWindow.h hunk are anchored on
byte-verified lines taken from a raw fetch of main@fe4f0a7. The runCommand
batch-branch hunk sits in a region whose fetched copy had elided line
wraps; its indentation is reconstructed to match the file's style (4
spaces at that nesting). `git apply` should take it as-is; if that ONE
hunk rejects, apply it by hand — it is a single added line
("batchSettings_ = settings;") placed directly after the existing
"partialSnapshot_ = gs::snapshot_output(pendingPartial_.toStdString());"
and directly before "gs::Settings one = settings;" in the Batch branch of
runCommand(). The other two hunks are exact.

Proof plan (Qt-class row — CI proves what a no-Qt sandbox cannot):

  * cmake build clean on linux + windows.
  * Offscreen harness batch cases (T4/T8/T9 family) unchanged-green —
    run 2..N argv now provably equal run-1 settings.
  * Sentinel (CI): no 'currentSettings()' call remains in
    onProcessFinished; batchSettings_ appears in MainWindow.h,
    runCommand (one write) and the continuation (one read).
  * Behavioural harness case T24 (sketch in the accompanying audit MD):
    two-file batch against a slow fake engine; mutate a SettingsPanel
    control programmatically between job 1 and job 2; assert job 2's argv
    (captured via the fake engine's argv log) equals job 1's. RED on main
    (job 2 reflects the mutation), green here.

After green CI proof: §5 row U-58 -> FIXED (harness: T24 (offscreen) +
sentinel), then check_docs.sh --emit + G10 base re-anchor.
---
 .../gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.cpp         | 14 ++++++++++++--
 .../gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.h           |  9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/working_code/gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.cpp b/working_code/gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.cpp
index 3333333..4444444 100644
--- a/working_code/gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.cpp
+++ b/working_code/gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.cpp
@@ -456,5 +456,11 @@ void MainWindow::runCommand() {
     gs::discard_partial(pendingPartial_.toStdString());  // self-heal a prior hard kill
     partialSnapshot_ = gs::snapshot_output(pendingPartial_.toStdString());
+    // U-58 / P1-38: freeze the settings for the WHOLE batch at start —
+    // every continuation job (onProcessFinished) builds its argv from this
+    // snapshot, never from a live currentSettings() re-read. The output
+    // plan above was computed and collision-checked against `settings`;
+    // the jobs must run with exactly those values.
+    batchSettings_ = settings;
     gs::Settings one = settings;
     one.mode = gs::Mode::Auto;  // single-file, no -b needed
     one.inputs = {in.toStdString()};
@@ -572,7 +578,11 @@ void MainWindow::onProcessFinished(int exitCode, QProcess::ExitStatus status) {
       gs::discard_partial(pendingPartial_.toStdString());
       partialSnapshot_ = gs::snapshot_output(pendingPartial_.toStdString());
-      auto settings = currentSettings();
-      gs::Settings one = settings;
+      // U-58 / P1-38: continuation jobs MUST come from the batch-start
+      // snapshot frozen into batchSettings_ (runCommand), never from a
+      // live currentSettings() — the plan was computed and collision-
+      // checked against THOSE settings; re-reading here rebuilds argv
+      // from state the plan never saw.
+      gs::Settings one = batchSettings_;
       one.mode = gs::Mode::Auto;
       one.inputs = {in.toStdString()};
       one.output = pendingPartial_.toStdString();
diff --git a/working_code/gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.h b/working_code/gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.h
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/working_code/gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.h
+++ b/working_code/gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.h
@@ -164,6 +164,15 @@ class MainWindow : public QMainWindow {
   QStringList batchTargets_;           // planned per-file outputs (audit U-01)
   int batchIndex_ = -1;
   QStringList batchQueue_;
+  // U-58 / P1-38 (F:NF-01): the settings the batch was STARTED with. Batch
+  // continuation jobs (onProcessFinished) used to call currentSettings()
+  // live, so any Actions-tab state that changed mid-batch silently altered
+  // every job after the first — the settings-twin of U-45's closed
+  // destination hole: an unplanned mutation of a job plan that was computed
+  // and collision-checked against DIFFERENT values. Written once in
+  // runCommand()'s batch branch, read only while batchIndex_ >= 0.
+  gs::Settings batchSettings_;
   gs::Mode batchMode_ = gs::Mode::Batch;
   // Explode frame verification (audit U-17 / P1-19): pre-run snapshot of the
   // files under the frame prefix, so onProcessFinished can tell frames THIS
